{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-11-Jul-2024-Shift4.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "The following bar graph represents the total number of students enrolled and the number of students who got campus placement in six different engineering colleges A, B, C, D, E, and F. Study the graph carefully and answer the question given below: What per cent (correct up to two decimal places) of total enrolled students have got campus placements in colleges A, C, and F?", "options": [{"text": "86.67%", "added": false}, {"text": "77.78%", "added": false}, {"text": "82.78%", "added": false}, {"text": "79.67%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "In ΔABC,D and E are points on sides AB and AC, such that DE∥ BC. If AD = x,DB = x - 3,AE = x + 3 and EC = x - 2, then the value of x is:", "options": [{"text": "5.2", "added": false}, {"text": "4.0", "added": false}, {"text": "4.5", "added": false}, {"text": "4.2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "In an obtuse-angled triangle ABC, the length of its longest side AB is 50 cm and one of the other two sides is 42 cm. If the area of the triangle is 294 cm2, what is the length (in cm) of its third side?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "Two wheelers", "added": false}, {"text": "Commercial vehicles", "added": false}, {"text": "Passenger vehicles", "added": false}, {"text": "Two wheelers and Passenger vehicles", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "Tom travelled 285 km in 6 hours. In his total travelling, he travelled the first part by bus at 40 km/hr and the remaining part by train at 55 km/hr. How much distance has he travelled by train?", "options": [{"text": "155 km", "added": false}, {"text": "120 km", "added": false}, {"text": "165 km", "added": false}, {"text": "135 km", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "The average of 50 numbers is 23. If each number is multiplied by 13, then the new average is:", "options": [{"text": "219", "added": false}, {"text": "299", "added": false}, {"text": "650", "added": false}, {"text": "88", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "replacement-effect", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "20.36 m", "added": false}, {"text": "22.32 m", "added": false}, {"text": "24.36 m", "added": false}, {"text": "26.32 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "How much simple interest will ₹5,000 earn in 14 months at a 12% interest rate per annum?", "options": [{"text": "₹600", "added": false}, {"text": "₹800", "added": false}, {"text": "₹700", "added": false}, {"text": "₹500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "Refer to the bar graph below and answer the question that follows. What is the difference between the number of students enrolled in Institute A in 2015 and 2017 and that in Institute B in 2016, 2018 and 2019?", "options": [{"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "150", "added": false}, {"text": "75", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "If 10% of 24% of x is 240,then x = ?", "options": [{"text": "100", "added": false}, {"text": "1000", "added": false}, {"text": "10000", "added": false}, {"text": "100000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "The number 611611611611 is: (a)divisible by both 6 and 11 (b)neither divisible by 6 nor by 11 (c)divisible by 6 only (d)divisible by 11 only", "options": [{"text": "(d)", "added": false}, {"text":